{"scenario":"dts-tx-budget-127500","rows":["C-0103","C-0104","C-0888","C-0890","C-0891","D-0005","D-0017","C-1043","C-0106","K-0093","K-0094","K-0095","C-0880","C-0851","C-0853","C-0326","C-0575","C-0595","C-1050"],"source":"Ed4 C.7.5.4, p.C-113; K.3.2.5, p.K-12","description":"A transmission holds no more whole blocks than fit in 127.5 s; what does not fit waits for the node\u0027s next transmission.","config":{"local_address":"0.0.1.2","address_size":4,"csma":{"mode":"slotted","node_slot_position":1},"modem":{"preamble_ms":1000,"flush_ms":500,"waveforms":[{"wn":2,"interleaver":"long","block_bytes":100,"block_ms":10000}]}},"note":"Conn 1 binds SAP 5 for non-ARQ (service type tx_mode 2, no confirmation) and gets S_BIND_ACCEPTED with MTU 2048 (A-0041, A-0047). Each S_UNIDATA_REQUEST is to SAP 5, DELIVERY MODE default, TTL 0 (the 648000-unit default, so TTD = request time \u002B 1296000000 ms, A-0089, A-0091), and asks for no confirmation, so it produces no SIS output (A-0095). The CAS wraps the DATA S_PDU (priority, SAP 5 to SAP 5, TTD) in a DATA C_PDU (B-0297). Each D_PDU is type 7 NON-ARQ-DATA (C-0323, C-0575) with EOW 0, EMPTY (C-0398), address size 4, source 0.0.1.2, the whole C_PDU as its one segment (offset 0, C_PDU size = segment size, C-0343, C-0346), DELIVER IN ORDER clear (C-0333), C_PDU IDs allocated from 0 in placement order (C-0326, C-1040), and no pre-fill (D-0003). The air start of a D_PDU is the start of the block holding its first byte, preamble_ms \u002B block x block_ms (C-1043); EOT = ceil((duration_ms - air start) / 500) (C-0104, C-0891, D-0005, D-0017), and the reception window is the same value because every copy of the C_PDU is in this transmission (C-0350, C-0352). The waveform is drc.default_speed, wn 2 long (C-0894). Three 400-byte U_PDUs, equal priority, each a 431-byte D_PDU. Fixture: preamble 1000, flush 500, 100 bytes and 10000 ms a block, so 127500 ms holds (127500 - 1500) / 10000 = 12 blocks, 1200 bytes (dts.max_transmission_ms is the default 127500). Two D_PDUs (862 bytes) fit, the third does not, so it waits (C-0880, K-0093). First burst 91500 ms, EOTs 181 and 101. After our own transmission: LBT 3000 (K-0074), slotted position 1 after our own transmission waits 1 slot (K-0082). Second burst 51500 ms, EOT 101, C_PDU ID 2. Since corpus 0.7.0 the DTS also keeps dts.ttd at the earliest TTD in its transmit queue: started when a request becomes the earliest, cancelled when the transmit queue empties (C-1050)."}
